{
  "group": "void",
  "upstream": "sanitize-html@2.17.6",
  "note": "Void elements and end-tag recovery. Whether an element can have content is a property of HTML, not of the policy: Options.SelfClosing only decides whether the element is written as \"<x />\" or as \"<x></x>\". Getting this wrong is how a sanitizer ends up emitting unbalanced markup that escapes its container.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "void-area",
      "fn": "sanitize",
      "args": [
        "<area>x",
        {
          "allowedTags": [
            "area"
          ],
          "selfClosing": []
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "sanitizeHtml",
      "goFn": "sanitizehtml.Sanitize",
      "note": "with nothing in selfClosing the void element is closed by an explicit end tag, immediately, before the following text"
    },
    {
